      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the greatest common factor (GCF) of 40 and 48, we can use the prime factorization method. Here are the steps:\n\n1. **Find the prime factorization of each number:**\n\n   - For 40:\n     \\[\n     40 = 2 \\times 20 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 10 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 5 = 2^3 \\times 5\n     \\]\n     So, the prime factorization of 40 is \\(2^3 \\times 5\\).\n\n   - For 48:\n     \\[\n     48 = 2 \\times 24 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 12 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 6 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 3 = 2^4 \\times 3\n     \\]\n     So, the prime factorization of 48 is \\(2^4 \\times 3\\).\n\n2. **Identify the common prime factors and their lowest powers:**\n   - The prime factorization of 40 is \\(2^3 \\times 5\\).\n   - The prime factorization of 48 is \\(2^4 \\times 3\\).\n   - The common prime factor is 2, and the lowest power of 2 that appears in both factorizations is \\(2^3\\).\n\n3. **Multiply the common prime factors with their lowest powers to find the GCF:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{GCF} = 2^3 = 8\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the greatest common factor of 40 and 48 is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).",
